  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "On moving from left to right across a period, the electron affinity becomes more negative. On moving from top to bottom in a group, the electron affinity becomes less negative.\nChlorine has more negative electron affinity than fluorine, Because adding an electron to fluorine ( $2 p$ orbital) causes greater repulsion than adding an electron to chlorine $(3 p$ orbital) which is larger in size.",
    "image": null
  },
